course: dictionary
lesson: 11488
title: Starting afresh
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Afresh is a small word with a big job. It means you begin again from the start, and you do it in a new way. «The rain washed the mud away, so the gardener could start afresh.» The old mess is gone, and the gardener is beginning the work again from the beginning.
explain: Look at the clues in the sentence. The mud was washed away, so the old mess has gone. Afresh tells you there is a new start. Try swapping in "from the beginning again". If the sentence still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
explain: Afresh can also mean looking at something in a new way. «Sam was stuck on his sum, so he looked at it afresh.» Sam did not just try the same thing harder. He saw the problem with new eyes, and that helped him solve it.
explain: Afresh often goes with start, begin or look: start afresh, begin afresh, look at something afresh. The verb tells you what is happening, and afresh tells you how it happens.
fact: Afresh is an adverb, so it tells you how something is done.
fact: «Afresh» means again from the beginning, or in a new way.
fact: «Afresh» can also mean once more, newly, as in «the old wall was painted afresh».
fact: Common phrases with afresh are start afresh, begin afresh and look at something afresh.
fact: When your work goes wrong at school, you can begin afresh on a clean page.
exercise: «After the spilt paint, Mia decided to begin the picture afresh.» What does afresh mean here? | Sadly, with a frown | Without any paint at all | Very quickly and messily | *From the beginning, in a new way
exercise: «Tom read the old map afresh and found the right path.» Why did Tom read the map afresh? | He read it only once and gave up | He put the map away for good | *He looked at it again with new eyes | He tore the map up
exercise: Which phrase means to start again from the beginning? | *Start afresh | Shout loudly | Sleep in late | Run home
test: «Ben's tower fell down, so he decided to build it afresh.» What does afresh tell us? | Ben gave the tower to his sister | Ben forgot to build anything | Ben built it quickly and carelessly | *Ben built it again from the start
test: Which word is closest in meaning to afresh? | *Anew | Slowly | Ago | Inside
exam: «After the storm, the villagers rebuilt their homes afresh.» What does afresh mean in this sentence? | *Again, from the beginning | Far away from home | Very tired and sleepy | In the middle of the storm
